    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Methodist Mission in Shawnee spanned 2,000 acres and housed 16 buildings where thousands of Indians learned farming and trades until 1862.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofshawnee.org/499/Community-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "On October 17, 1862, William Quantrill raided Shawnee, burning the town in a brutal Civil War skirmish.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofshawnee.org/499/Community-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Between 1860 and 1862, the Pony Express operated in Kansas, with eleven stations including one in Shawnee along the route.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cityofshawnee.org/499/Community-History"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Shawnee was officially laid out as a town in 1857, marking its formal establishment within Johnson County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
